message: "If you use this research artifact, please cite it using the metadata below. For the original Apart Research Sprint submission, see CITATION.bib."
title: "What Should We Check Next? An Auditable Ambiguity-Preserving Investigator for AI Incidents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Thorstensen
    given-names: Linda
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1588-7309"
year: 2026
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lydia-No/ai-incident-evidence-selection"
url: "https://apartresearch.com/sprints/projects/what-should-we-check-next-testing-ambiguitypreserving-evidence-selection-for-ai-incident-investigation-5nv4"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility and research artifact for an ambiguity-preserving AI incident
  investigator that maintains compatible explanations, exposes unresolved and
  model-gap states, and selects discriminating evidence checks using a frozen,
  auditable rule. The repository contains the implementation, frozen synthetic
  evaluation, provenance, verification materials, and a source-bounded
  real-incident operational handoff.
keywords:
  - AI incident response
  - incident investigation
  - active diagnosis
  - ambiguity preservation
  - evidence selection
  - reproducibility
